(vis:=b/'visualizations'/'index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Controlled collagen-inspired network comparisons</title><style>body{max-width:1100px;margin:30px auto;background:#101d2a;color:#e9eff4;font:17px system-ui;padding:20px}a{color:#63d8ba}img{max-width:100%;height:auto}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #456}table{border-collapse:collapse}</style><h1>Matched stiffness, different network architectures</h1><p>Executed central-force surrogate. No tissue calibration. Ten seeds; both equal-material and matched intact axial K. Shear held out. The disordered family has geometric disorder on an FCC graph.</p><p><a href="../RESULTS.md">Full methods/results and numerical caveats</a> · <a href="fenicsx-table.html">Explore all 1,600 FEniCSx comparisons</a> · <a href="../MANIFEST.json">SHA-256 manifest</a></p><img src="event-network-work-tension.svg"><img src="event-network-work-shear.svg"><p>Means include work to strain limit for censored cases; see counts below. Those values are not known failure work.</p>'+table+'<h2>Animations: seed 101</h2><p>Left: triangular 2D; middle: FCC 3D; right: geometrically disordered FCC 3D. A panel freezes at failure. Pace is illustrative, not physical time. Dark red: removed edges; label gives actual strain and removed count.</p>'+imgs+'<h2>FEniCSx numerical acceptance</h2><p>Saved-data reanalysis, not new solves. Acceptance is a numerical gate, not toughness.</p><a href="fenicsx-table.html"><img src="fenicsx-acceptance.svg"></a>')
